Error [jet.ValueNotSendable]: `spawn_with` moves its `T` into a task, and here `T` is `Cell<Int>`, which isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/concurrency_boundaries/generic_task_spawn_rejects_a_thread_confined_argument.jet:8:39
    |
  8 | share: fn(cell: &&Cell<Int>) -> Int { spawn_with(cell) }
    |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `Cell` owns thread-local state and must stay on the thread that created it; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: Call `spawn_with` with plain owned data, or share state through `Shared<T>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1102
